│  Failed Delivery Attempts                                                   │
│  The carrier makes up to 3 delivery attempts at the registered address. If  │
│  all 3 attempts                                                             │
│  fail (no one available to receive the package), the order is held at the   │
│  local distribution                                                         │
│  center for 7 calendar days. If not picked up within that window, it is     │
│  returned to our                                                            │
│  warehouse and the customer is contacted to arrange a new delivery (a new   │
│  shipping fee may                                                           │
│  apply) or a refund.                                                        │
│                                                                             │
│  ---                                                                        │
│                                                                             │
│  Source: delivery_faq.md                                                    │
│  Frequently Asked Questions — Delivery                                      │
│  - Q: Can I change the delivery address after placing the order?            │
│    A: Only before the order is dispatched. Once a tracking code is issued,  │
│  the address is                                                             │
│    locked for that shipment.                                                │
│  - Q: What happens if I miss all delivery attempts?                         │
│    A: After 3 failed attempts, the package is held at the local             │
│  distribution center for 7                                                  │
│    days, then returned to our warehouse if not picked up.                   │
│  - Q: Do you ship to PO boxes?                                              │
│    A: No. We ship to residential and business addresses, including          │
│  apartment lockers or                                                       │
│    concierge services for standard-sized packages.                          │
│  - Q: My package arrived damaged. What do I do?                             │
│    A: Take photos of the damage and packaging within 48 hours and contact   │
│  support with your                                                          │
│    order number. Approved claims get a free replacement or refund without   │
│  the standard return                                                        │
│    process.                                                                 │
│  - Q: Why did I receive two tracking codes for one order?                   │
│    A: Orders with items from different warehouses may ship as separate      │
│  packages, each with                                                        │
│    its own tracking code, possibly dispatched at different times.           │
│  - Q: Is express/expedited shipping available?                              │
│    A: Express shipping is not currently offered. All orders follow the      │
│  standard timeframes:                                                       │
│    5–10 business days domestic, 15–30 business days international.          │
│  - Q: Who pays for re-shipping if I entered the wrong address?              │
│    A: The customer covers the re-shipping cost if the address error was     │
│  provided by the                                                            │
│    customer. If the error originated from our system, re-shipping is free.  │
│                                                                             │
│  ---                                                                        │
│                                                                             │
│  Source: specific_delivery_cases.md                                         │
│  Address Change After Order Placement                                       │
│  An address change request is only possible before the order is             │
│  dispatched. Once a tracking                                                │
│  code has been issued, the address can no longer be changed; the customer   │
│  must wait for the                                                          │
│  delivery attempt or contact support after a failed attempt to arrange      │
│  redirection through                                                        │
│  the carrier, where available.                                              │
│                                                                             │
